@startuml
title Incident Lifecycle — State Pattern (illegal transitions are impossible)
skinparam stateBackgroundColor #EEF4FF
skinparam stateBorderColor #3B5BA9
[*] --> NEW : report
NEW --> CLASSIFIED : classify\n(auto or manual)
CLASSIFIED --> CLASSIFIED : re-classify
CLASSIFIED --> ASSIGNED : assign
ASSIGNED --> ASSIGNED : reassign
ASSIGNED --> ACKNOWLEDGED : acknowledge\n(response SLA met?)
ACKNOWLEDGED --> ASSIGNED : reassign
ACKNOWLEDGED --> IN_PROGRESS : start work
IN_PROGRESS --> AWAITING_INFO : request info
AWAITING_INFO --> IN_PROGRESS : reporter answers
IN_PROGRESS --> ASSIGNED : escalate / hand over
IN_PROGRESS --> RESOLVED : resolve\n(fix + root cause)
RESOLVED --> VERIFIED : reporter verifies
RESOLVED --> REOPENED : reopen
VERIFIED --> REOPENED : reopen
REOPENED --> ASSIGNED : sticky reassignment
RESOLVED --> CLOSED : auto-close after 72h
VERIFIED --> CLOSED : close
CLOSED --> [*]

note right of AWAITING_INFO : SLA clock PAUSED
note left of NEW : NEW → CLOSED is rejected:\nNewState only overrides classify()
@enduml
